 **Design:** [system-design.md#contracts](system-design.md#contracts)
 
+### Specialty directory
+
+<a id="req-vet-003"></a>
+
+The veterinarian directory answers which specialties a veterinarian holds; staff also ask the inverse, which veterinarians hold a specialty. A read-only page answers it: every specialty the clinic knows, by its stored name, each with the veterinarians holding it `[REQ-VET-003]`. Each veterinarian appears by full name, first name then last name. A veterinarian holding no specialty appears under none, because the page lists specialties rather than the full roster. Every specialty is on one page, with no paging. The page is reached by its own address only; no navigation entry or link from another page leads to it.
+
+**Done when:**
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given the clinic's specialties, when the specialty directory is opened, then every specialty is listed by its stored name with the veterinarians holding it.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given a veterinarian, when they are listed under a specialty, then they are shown by first name followed by last name.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given a veterinarian holding several specialties, when the specialty directory is opened, then they are listed under each one.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given a veterinarian holding no specialty, when the specialty directory is opened, then that veterinarian does not appear.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given any number of specialties, when the specialty directory is opened, then all of them are shown on one page.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given the other pages of the system, when they are rendered, then none carries a navigation entry or link to the specialty directory.
+
+**Edge cases:**
+1. A specialty held by no veterinarian is still listed, and is shown as held by none rather than left blank.
+2. Specialties, and the veterinarians under each, are presented in a stable order rather than an arbitrary one.
+3. A clinic with no specialties shows the page with an empty listing rather than failing.
+4. The page's own wording follows the reader's language; a specialty's stored name is shown as stored.
+
